I've successfully identified and fixed the bug in the `advanceTurn` function in `src/sim.ts`. 

## Problem Summary
The issue was that population was incorrectly growing even in settlements that were breaking even on food (zero surplus), when it should only grow when there's an actual food surplus.

## Root Cause
In the `advanceTurn` function, the condition `if (foodSurplus >= 0)` caused population to increase whenever there was a food surplus OR exactly zero surplus. 

## Fix Applied
Changed line 43 in `/Users/tijs/projects/local-model-bench/runner/runs/tmp5en9n4q_/run/src/sim.ts` from:
```typescript
if (foodSurplus >= 0) {
```
to:
```typescript
if (foodSurplus > 0) {
```

This ensures population only grows when there's an actual positive food surplus.

## Verification
- All existing tests continue to pass
- Added new test cases specifically verifying the fix for the edge case where food production equals consumption
- The fix correctly handles the scenario described in the bug report

The change is minimal and targeted, addressing exactly the issue described while maintaining all existing functionality.


